    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Marco’s fictional profile reports no driving ability: Marco <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="can’t" data-hint="No driving ability requires the negative modal can’t before the base verb drive." data-fix="Marco can’t drive, so he takes the bus to work." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> drive, so he takes the bus to work. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(can)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The map places the pharmacy in the middle, with the bank on one side and the café on the other: It is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="between" data-hint="One place in the middle of two named reference points takes between." data-fix="The pharmacy is between the bank and the café." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> the bank and the café. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(prepositions of place)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
