  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real home, route, cooking, devices, contacts, schedule, workplace, health, or travel plans. Use the fictional map, interface card, community center, or conference scenario below whenever you prefer.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Map route:</b> Guide a fictional visitor from the station to a public venue. Use three ordered positive steps and one route to avoid.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Interface card:</b> Explain how to change one setting on an invented app. Keep one main action in each step and finish with a saving instruction.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Safety station:</b> Give one calm rule and one urgent warning. Deliver the grammar accurately while changing the strength of your voice.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Request choice:</b> Turn <span class="ex">Send me the file</span> into an appropriate request to a fictional coworker who can reasonably refuse.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Shared plan:</b> Make two fictional event suggestions with <span class="ex">let’s</span> and one shared action to avoid with <span class="ex">let’s not</span>.</div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: orient a fictional conference visitor</h3>
    <p>Give a 45–60 second arrival and welcome message. Include all six pieces of evidence:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>three ordered positive instructions with <span class="ex">first, next,</span> and <span class="ex">finally</span>;</li>
      <li>one negative safety instruction with <span class="ex">don’t</span> or formal <span class="ex">do not</span>;</li>
      <li>one warm offer or encouragement;</li>
      <li>one request with <span class="ex">Can you…?</span> because the listener has a real choice;</li>
      <li>one shared suggestion with <span class="ex">let’s</span> and one with <span class="ex">let’s not</span>;</li>
      <li>three distinct deliveries: calm instruction, warm welcome, and firm urgent warning.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The listener follows the route on a fictional map and labels each social action. Revise any step whose form, order, or voice creates a different action from the one you intended.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “An ordinary instruction starts with the ______ verb and normally leaves the listener ______ unspoken. For the negative, I start with ______. I can soften an instruction with ______, but a request question may give more choice. For a shared plan, I start with ______.”</p>
    <p>Then use a fictional map to give one calm direction, one urgent warning with <span class="ex">don’t</span>, and one inclusive suggestion with <span class="ex">let’s</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You matched base and negative forms, shared suggestions, request choices, understood subjects, offers, and supportive instructions to explicit contexts.">
    <h3>Final quiz: imperative form and tone</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
